sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch09-15> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "A network corresponds to ordinary d-dimensional space exactly when the number of nodes within graph distance r of a node grows in a limiting sense like r^d; tree-like or randomly connected networks correspond to no finite dimension.";
    dc:type "mathematical";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Network dimension is set by growth of node counts with distance";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 9, “Fundamental Physics”; section “Space as a Network” (from p. 475), p. 478. Scope: large networks and their correspondence to finite-dimensional space"
}
